HuffmanThree Class Documentation
-------------------------------------------------
1. Class responsibility
The HuffmanTree class will be responsible for:
    1. Building a Huffman tree from character frequencies.
    2. Using your custom MyPriorityQueue (binary Min-Heap).
    3. Combining nodes according to their frequencies.
    4. Maintaining the final root node.
    5. Providing access to the completed tree.

The algorithm follows these steps:
    1. Create a leaf node for every character and its frequency.
    2. Insert all leaf nodes into your Min-Priority Queue.
    3. Extract the two nodes with the smallest frequencies.
    4. Create a new internal node whose frequency is the sum of those two frequencies.
    5. Make the two extracted nodes its children.
    6. Insert the new internal node back into the priority queue.
    7. Repeat until only one node remains.
    8. That remaining node becomes the root of the Huffman tree.


2) Attribute
    - root (HuffmanNode) : Store the root of the tree.

2) Method
    a) HuffmanTree() constructor
        - Receive any argument
        - Set the Huffman node to null

    b) buildTree()
        1. Receive the HashMap containing symbols and frequencies.
        2. Iterate through the entries.
        3. Create a leaf HuffmanNode for each entry.
        4. Insert each leaf into your custom MyPriorityQueue.
        5. Combines the two smallest nodes into internal nodes.
        6. Repeats until one node remains.
        7. Assigns that final node to root.

    3) isEmpty() : Just check if the tree is empty or not.

    4) getRoot() : Return the root value.
